       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about double the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals**: 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** at a different frequency.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm it and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was verified. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter that."
