       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the dose, and 5,100 mg/day is about twice the labeled maximum for metformin. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and no standard indication calls for this dose. The harm, mainly lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, could be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can enter 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) right away, or another dose you choose.\n- **Go through pharmacy or a second prescriber.** If there's a documented reason to exceed the maximum, such as a protocol or specialist recommendation, a pharmacist or attending can review it and enter it directly. That review is the right safeguard for an off-label dose like this.\n- **Check for a typo.** Please confirm that 1700 mg wasn't meant to be 850 mg or 1000 mg.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
